00:51:55,120 --> 00:51:55,953
Looks

558
00:52:06,980 --> 00:52:09,497
like our epic journey together has come to
an end.

559
00:52:09,580 --> 00:52:11,480
I'm sorry to hear that, Fang.

560
00:52:29,180 --> 00:52:31,140
Our journey continues, Selene.

561
00:52:31,340 --> 00:52:33,281
I'm delighted to hear that, Fang.

562
00:52:34,020 --> 00:52:34,853
Shit.

563
00:52:39,280 --> 00:52:42,926
We are now into the
fifth hour of this chase

564
00:52:42,927 --> 00:52:45,980
and roughly 30 miles
into northeastern Texas.

565
00:52:45,981 --> 00:52:50,040
CNN has learned that the driver,
former U.S.

566
00:52:50,041 --> 00:52:53,495
Army Captain Ryan Flanagan,
was a decorated Green

567
00:52:53,496 --> 00:52:56,600
Beret, wounded multiple
times during combat operations.

568
00:52:56,601 --> 00:52:57,977
He'll never turn himself in.

569
00:52:58,060 --> 00:53:00,517
Sounded like you two still have a
connection.

570
00:53:00,600 --> 00:53:01,857
Why'd you divorce him?

571
00:53:01,940 --> 00:53:02,840
Oh, let me see.

572
00:53:02,980 --> 00:53:04,520
Thinking back on it...

573
00:53:05,260 --> 00:53:06,093
Hmm.

574
00:53:06,200 --> 00:53:07,877
None of your fucking business.

575
00:53:07,960 --> 00:53:11,680
Look, we need all the help we can,
and time is not on our side.

576
00:53:11,840 --> 00:53:13,428
Yeah, you mean on his side.

577
00:53:15,980 --> 00:53:19,279
The FBI continues to issue
brief general statements

578
00:53:19,280 --> 00:53:22,660
that they are closely
monitoring the situation...

579
00:53:22,661 --> 00:53:29,140
Okay, when he came back that last time,
things were really good for a while.

580
00:53:29,820 --> 00:53:32,564
We were older, things felt more clear, but

581
00:53:32,565 --> 00:53:35,080
something happened when he was over there.

582
00:53:35,140 --> 00:53:36,081
He was captured.

583
00:53:36,820 --> 00:53:38,420
And he was broken.

584
00:53:42,370 --> 00:53:45,230
Do you understand what he sacrificed?

585
00:53:54,470 --> 00:53:55,310
Hey.

586
00:53:55,311 --> 00:53:56,710
What's between us?

587
00:53:56,870 --> 00:53:57,827
What's between us?

588
00:53:57,910 --> 00:54:03,830
The Pentagon has confirmed that Captain
Ryan Flanagan, a Bronze Star recipient and

589
00:54:03,831 --> 00:54:08,790
multiple Purple Heart honoree,
was honorably discharged in 2005,

590
00:54:09,230 --> 00:54:11,150
having served with distinction.

591
00:54:11,890 --> 00:54:15,470
Wiz's real name was Wade Melvie.

592
00:54:15,730 --> 00:54:19,870
He was a Master Sergeant in Captain
Flanagan's Special Forces Unit.

593
00:54:20,070 --> 00:54:24,210
In their final tour in Afghanistan,
their helicopter was shot down,

594
00:54:24,410 --> 00:54:25,907
and the unit was captured.

595
00:54:25,990 --> 00:54:29,150
During their escape, Melvie was killed.

596
00:54:34,760 --> 00:54:38,188
Captain Flanagan and the
surviving members of the unit

597
00:54:38,189 --> 00:54:41,230
served as pallbearers at
Sergeant Melvie's funeral.

598
00:54:42,260 --> 00:54:48,880
The saying, never leave a man behind,
is a deeply ingrained principle in the

599
00:54:48,881 --> 00:54:51,880
military, especially within Special
Forces.

600
00:54:52,500 --> 00:54:56,485
This sentiment is a powerful
cultural force within the

601
00:54:56,486 --> 00:55:01,020
Armed Services and fosters a
strong sense of responsibility.

602
00:55:01,920 --> 00:55:08,080
It appears that application is still
standing even in this complex scenario.

603
00:55:16,220 --> 00:55:19,000
Does Arkansas already miss me,
Major Tilton?

604
00:55:19,300 --> 00:55:23,520
This is Major Walter Pope, Commander of
Texas Highway Patrol.

605
00:55:23,920 --> 00:55:25,260
I stand corrected.

606
00:55:25,261 --> 00:55:27,849
Thanks for the welcome mat back there,
Major.

607
00:55:27,960 --> 00:55:32,141
Well, now, Captain
Flanagan, y'all better stop this

608
00:55:32,142 --> 00:55:35,697
nonsense or things are gonna
get a whole lot worse for you.

609
00:55:35,780 --> 00:55:40,060
Sounds like a threat, and I tend to
respond aggressively to those.

610
00:55:40,500 --> 00:55:45,842
In my state, when a suspect
resists arrest in a vehicle, law

611
00:55:45,843 --> 00:55:49,777
enforcement's within their
rights to open fire on that vehicle.

612
00:55:49,860 --> 00:55:53,720
Texas, where the entire state sports a
collective hard-on.

613
00:55:53,721 --> 00:55:55,250
Every time a gun is fired.

614
00:55:57,600 --> 00:56:03,400
Well, as I'm sure you know from combat,
whenever rifle fire is involved,

615
00:56:04,380 --> 00:56:06,780
stray bullets are always a possibility.

616
00:56:07,260 --> 00:56:09,540
Listen to me, you inbred dung farmer.

617
00:56:10,020 --> 00:56:13,000
I've been ducking small arms fire most of
my life.

618
00:56:13,680 --> 00:56:18,380
So if you can rip yourself away from
scraping off roadkill along the interstate

619
00:56:18,381 --> 00:56:22,540
long enough to join the hunt, please,
bring it on.

620
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:24,833
No.

621
00:56:26,040 --> 00:56:27,600
I will, Flanagan.

622
00:56:28,700 --> 00:56:29,960
I surely will.

623
00:56:30,260 --> 00:56:31,160
Call ended.

624
00:56:32,440 --> 00:56:35,620
Helene, can you make the car's phone
untraceable?

625
00:56:35,980 --> 00:56:37,020
Certainly, Fang.

626
00:56:39,640 --> 00:56:42,522
The vehicle's phone tracking has gone
dead, Major.

627
00:56:44,100 --> 00:56:46,512
Why aren't we tracking his personal cell?

628
00:56:46,680 --> 00:56:47,915
Haven't been able to.

629
00:56:48,000 --> 00:56:50,529
He must have a burner or an unplugged
phone.

630
00:56:50,620 --> 00:56:51,500
He's smart.

631
00:56:51,840 --> 00:56:52,899
We'll keep trying.

632
00:57:40,200 --> 00:57:40,680
Tell Swat.

633
00:57:40,681 --> 00:57:42,920
By the before you...
by before you let them.

634
00:58:36,180 --> 00:58:37,013
Is

635
00:58:48,970 --> 00:58:50,810
that a God damn news chopper?

636
00:58:50,890 --> 00:58:52,125
I can't confirm, sir.

637
00:59:02,120 --> 00:59:02,600
Norm.

638
00:59:02,740 --> 00:59:04,799
Give me a still frame to that shot.

639
00:59:06,720 --> 00:59:07,553
Bingo.

640
00:59:12,870 --> 00:59:13,770
Tell Swat.

641
00:59:13,870 --> 00:59:15,607
If that's the one, That bird is impeding
them.

642
00:59:15,690 --> 00:59:17,161
They are clear to engage.

643
00:59:17,390 --> 00:59:19,130
Sir, should we try to make contact first?

644
00:59:19,210 --> 00:59:20,490
I mean, the entire country is watching.

645
00:59:20,491 --> 00:59:22,726
We are about to make contact, Captain.

646
00:59:28,960 --> 00:59:30,254
Tanker, where are you?

647
00:59:30,660 --> 00:59:31,560
Above you.

648
00:59:35,900 --> 00:59:37,488
You're flying that gazelle?

649
00:59:38,100 --> 00:59:39,820
Munches, like a madman.

650
00:59:40,140 --> 00:59:40,973
Hey, buddy.

651
00:59:41,260 --> 00:59:42,093
Hey, pal.

652
00:59:42,220 --> 00:59:44,840
Hey, I don't want you guys getting mixed
up in this.

653
00:59:44,841 --> 00:59:46,723
A little late for that, Captain.

654
00:59:46,880 --> 00:59:50,000
We'll keep the birds off you for as long
as we can.

655
00:59:50,220 --> 00:59:52,200
Take evasive maneuvers.

656
00:59:52,320 --> 00:59:53,677
That's all I've been doing.

657
00:59:53,760 --> 00:59:56,940
Then I guess take more evasive maneuvers.

658
00:59:57,460 --> 00:59:58,560
Gotta go, brother.

659
01:00:09,000 --> 01:00:10,882
Helene, what's the closest city?

660
01:00:11,380 --> 01:00:13,440
One moment while I look that up.

661
01:00:14,900 --> 01:00:16,606
Where the hell's the suspect?

662
01:00:17,060 --> 01:00:18,766
You ordered a SWAT to engage.

663
01:00:18,960 --> 01:00:22,560
I, but, sir... I don't give a good
goddamn if the cameras see it.

664
01:00:22,640 --> 01:00:24,169
That's felony obstruction.

665
01:00:26,000 --> 01:00:30,700
Tyler, population 100,223.

666
01:00:36,600 --> 01:00:38,360
I think they're green-lit.

667
01:00:50,290 --> 01:00:54,055
I'm gonna need you to find a certain kind
of establishment there.

668
01:01:04,540 --> 01:01:06,716
Somebody get a visual on the suspect.

669
01:01:10,500 --> 01:01:11,680
Kick-ass!

670
01:01:18,180 --> 01:01:21,340
The Special Forces are often described as
the most powerful force in the world.

671
01:01:21,341 --> 01:01:26,106
But what's said by military planners is
the tip of the spear in combat operations.

672
01:01:26,300 --> 01:01:30,880
A recent VA study published in the New
England Journal of Medicine found that

673
01:01:30,881 --> 01:01:34,161
special operations soldiers suffer from

674
01:01:34,203 --> 01:01:38,034
PTSD after combat
at nearly twice the rate.

675
01:01:43,900 --> 01:01:47,222
Shows of support for
Flanagan are appearing across

676
01:01:47,223 --> 01:01:50,620
all social media platforms,
urging police restraint.

677
01:01:50,621 --> 01:01:53,060
In any efforts to apprehend him.

678
01:01:53,120 --> 01:01:56,755
We're seeing scores of
viral posts from all over

679
01:01:56,756 --> 01:02:00,120
the country, from veterans
to college students.

680
01:02:03,500 --> 01:02:04,333
Hi.

681
01:02:04,420 --> 01:02:05,760
Good afternoon.

682
01:02:07,700 --> 01:02:09,540
You all do paint jobs?

683
01:02:10,780 --> 01:02:11,700
Yeah.

684
01:02:13,380 --> 01:02:17,100
What does that cost, typically?

685
01:02:28,890 --> 01:02:30,490
Running a one-day special.

686
01:02:31,710 --> 01:02:32,543
Free.

687
01:02:33,090 --> 01:02:33,950
For anybody.

688
01:02:35,790 --> 01:02:37,672
You shed blood for this country.

689
01:02:40,170 --> 01:02:42,170
Let's get that leg taken care of.

690
01:02:42,570 --> 01:02:43,403
Follow me.

691
01:02:58,070 --> 01:02:59,770
Munch, is that an airport?

692
01:03:02,630 --> 01:03:03,990
They can't follow.

693
01:03:19,120 --> 01:03:20,640
Dude, I think we're hit.

694
01:03:22,000 --> 01:03:23,500
Control, Black Hawk 7.

695
01:03:23,720 --> 01:03:25,020
Target neutralized.

696
01:03:26,800 --> 01:03:29,212
Sending ground units to Walters Airfield.

697
01:04:16,000 --> 01:04:17,588
Hey, Tanker, you all right?

698
01:04:18,040 --> 01:04:19,040
Yeah, I'm okay.

699
01:04:22,480 --> 01:04:26,440
I don't want to mention to you how much I
hate jail.

700
01:04:27,200 --> 01:04:28,965
We're not out of the game yet.

701
01:04:33,070 --> 01:04:34,776
You got a credit card on you?

702
01:04:49,360 --> 01:04:49,840
Wow.

703
01:04:50,160 --> 01:04:54,880
You took the liberty of changing out your
plates for the clean Texas Tech.

704
01:04:55,680 --> 01:04:59,037
Sure as hell ain't gonna hide this dragon
for too much longer.

705
01:04:59,120 --> 01:05:00,040
It'll have to do.

706
01:05:00,041 --> 01:05:01,335
I'll take you to jail.

707
01:05:02,420 --> 01:05:05,200
A buddy of mine served in them.

708
01:05:06,140 --> 01:05:07,220
He helped you out.

709
01:05:09,500 --> 01:05:10,971
I can't thank you enough.

710
01:05:11,240 --> 01:05:13,416
We might have been in different wars.

711
01:05:14,260 --> 01:05:15,495
We're still brothers.

712
01:05:16,880 --> 01:05:18,480
You travel safe now.

713
01:05:38,140 --> 01:05:40,860
Oh Lord, I don't want to die in Texas.

714
01:05:41,240 --> 01:05:42,160
Come on, Tex!

715
01:05:42,320 --> 01:05:43,261
Sing it with me!

716
01:05:43,620 --> 01:05:47,180
We're the deer of the antelope plain.

717
01:05:55,440 --> 01:05:57,380
How in the hell did we lose him?

718
01:05:58,800 --> 01:05:59,760
It's impossible.

719
01:06:06,500 --> 01:06:08,441
Last list of registration, ma'am.

720
01:06:32,470 --> 01:06:37,640
The Kentucky State Police just released
the name of the victim at the crime scene.

721
01:06:37,760 --> 01:06:39,100
Captain Flanagan fled.

722
01:06:39,280 --> 01:06:45,800
He was Todd Ferris, a 58-year-old
prominent defense attorney in Louisville

723
01:06:45,801 --> 01:06:50,440
who has defended many high-profile
clients, including the ex-governor.

724
01:06:50,580 --> 01:06:55,640
The Louisville Courier released a story on
their website about 20 minutes ago citing

725
01:06:55,641 --> 01:07:03,100
an arrest report from 2004 charging Todd
Ferris with a multi-million dollar real

726
01:07:03,101 --> 01:07:06,040
estate fraud scheme that was later
dropped.

727
01:07:06,240 --> 01:07:08,080
The story goes on to say...

728
01:08:26,320 --> 01:08:27,280
Are you okay?

729
01:08:27,680 --> 01:08:29,460
Hey, are you okay?

730
01:08:29,680 --> 01:08:30,520
Are you okay?

731
01:08:31,860 --> 01:08:33,154
I've been ringing you.

732
01:08:33,780 --> 01:08:35,097
Tell me everything's okay.

733
01:08:35,180 --> 01:08:35,820
I'm fine.

734
01:08:35,980 --> 01:08:36,560
I'm fine.

735
01:08:36,720 --> 01:08:37,280
Uh-uh.

736
01:08:37,360 --> 01:08:38,640
I can hear it in your voice.

737
01:08:38,660 --> 01:08:40,072
Don't bullshit me, Ryan.

738
01:08:41,320 --> 01:08:42,153
Tara.

739
01:08:42,240 --> 01:08:42,860
I'm good.

740
01:08:43,140 --> 01:08:43,973
Where are you?

741
01:08:45,120 --> 01:08:46,000
Tyler, Texas.

742
01:08:46,700 --> 01:08:48,500
Which is charming, by the way.

743
01:08:48,700 --> 01:08:49,533
Oh my God.

744
01:08:49,720 --> 01:08:51,220
I was so worried that...

745
01:08:51,860 --> 01:08:55,160
The cameras lost you for six hours.

746
01:08:58,180 --> 01:08:59,020
Where are you?

747
01:09:00,000 --> 01:09:01,420
At my sister's.

748
01:09:02,620 --> 01:09:04,160
Also charming, by the way.

749
01:09:09,280 --> 01:09:10,113
Um...

750
01:09:13,210 --> 01:09:14,290
Tell me something.

751
01:09:18,540 --> 01:09:19,716
Was it self-defense?

752
01:09:24,120 --> 01:09:26,591
Feels like everything I do is
self-defense.

753
01:09:27,380 --> 01:09:28,968
That's not an answer, baby.

754
01:09:32,680 --> 01:09:36,340
I did everything I could not to hurt him.

755
01:09:36,440 --> 01:09:37,320
I promise.

756
01:09:38,020 --> 01:09:39,760
And he shot me in the leg.

757
01:09:40,020 --> 01:09:42,020
But it was him or me, Tara.

758
01:09:42,720 --> 01:09:43,620
I swear.

759
01:09:47,300 --> 01:09:48,771
Then I'm glad it was you.

760
01:09:57,060 --> 01:10:00,200
Hey, been thinking a lot about that beach.

761
01:10:00,880 --> 01:10:01,713
Beach?

762
01:10:01,800 --> 01:10:03,020
What beach?

763
01:10:04,420 --> 01:10:06,140
The one near Cancun.

764
01:10:06,860 --> 01:10:07,693
Remember?

765
01:10:07,920 --> 01:10:08,753
Oh.

766
01:10:09,720 --> 01:10:10,553
That beach.

767
01:10:21,480 --> 01:10:23,960
Locals called it La Mongosta.

768
01:10:24,280 --> 01:10:24,920
Yeah.

769
01:10:25,060 --> 01:10:26,420
The mongoose.

770
01:10:26,580 --> 01:10:26,760
Yeah.

771
01:10:27,440 --> 01:10:29,264
Why do they call it that again?

772
01:10:29,840 --> 01:10:30,860
No snakes.

773
01:10:33,400 --> 01:10:36,760
As I recall, we did some epic boning on
that beach.

774
01:10:38,900 --> 01:10:40,560
Indeed we did.

775
01:10:45,460 --> 01:10:46,660
You should go back.

776
01:10:52,520 --> 01:10:53,400
You mean it?

777
01:10:53,960 --> 01:10:54,420
Yeah.

778
01:10:54,560 --> 01:10:56,000
It's my retirement plan.

779
01:10:59,120 --> 01:10:59,580
Okay.

780
01:10:59,581 --> 01:11:00,699
I'll tell you what.

781
01:11:02,720 --> 01:11:06,320
You get to the mongoose, and we'll take
you from there.

782
01:11:15,080 --> 01:11:16,315
It's always been you.

783
01:11:16,760 --> 01:11:17,880
And only you.

784
01:11:18,440 --> 01:11:19,400
My whole life.

785
01:11:23,960 --> 01:11:25,140
And you for me.

786
01:12:06,800 --> 01:12:08,057
Yeah, just put it in park.

787
01:12:08,140 --> 01:12:08,973
Morning, Tim.

788
01:12:09,960 --> 01:12:10,897
What's happening?

789
01:12:10,980 --> 01:12:11,813
Roy.

790
01:12:12,240 --> 01:12:13,897
Looking for that runaway vet.

791
01:12:13,980 --> 01:12:15,156
He robbed Fort Knox.

792
01:12:15,640 --> 01:12:16,740
I just work here.

793
01:12:17,400 --> 01:12:19,357
Making your run down to San Antonio?

794
01:12:19,440 --> 01:12:20,273
Per usual.

795
01:12:22,240 --> 01:12:23,073
All right.

796
01:12:23,480 --> 01:12:24,715
Have a good one then.

797
01:12:49,210 --> 01:12:50,043
Thanks, Roy.

798
01:12:57,040 --> 01:12:57,880
Still hurting?

799
01:12:58,660 --> 01:12:59,520
I'll be okay.

800
01:13:01,120 --> 01:13:03,860
The guy shot me back in Kentucky.

801
01:13:03,861 --> 01:13:05,337
In case you were wondering.

802
01:13:05,420 --> 01:13:06,253
I wasn't.

803
01:13:06,780 --> 01:13:09,251
I'll let the state police know I seen you.

804
01:13:09,580 --> 01:13:10,933
Crossing into Oklahoma.

805
01:13:11,540 --> 01:13:14,217
Get a couple of dozen brother vet trucks
to call it in, too.

806
01:13:14,300 --> 01:13:18,006
By the end of the day, your mares will be
hunting you in Alaska.

807
01:13:18,860 --> 01:13:19,978
Thank you, brother.

808
01:13:22,220 --> 01:13:24,926
I was a POW in NAMM for three and a half
years.

809
01:13:26,760 --> 01:13:28,113
Guards used to hurt me.

810
01:13:29,320 --> 01:13:30,967
Everywhere you could figure.

811
01:13:33,100 --> 01:13:37,940
Whenever I can help out a brother vet,
I feel like I'm hurting them guards back.

812
01:13:39,580 --> 01:13:40,413
Just a little.

813
01:14:08,640 --> 01:14:09,900
That's Shelby, old hon.

814
01:14:09,920 --> 01:14:11,920
He's just crossed into New Mexico.

815
01:14:14,560 --> 01:14:15,900
I seen that Shelby.

816
01:14:16,180 --> 01:14:17,360
Near Shreveport.

817
01:14:20,160 --> 01:14:24,336
Yeah, that fan guy all over the news is
walking down the strip in Vegas.

818
01:14:38,940 --> 01:14:40,360
Got a call.

819
01:14:40,500 --> 01:14:42,206
He's headed back to Kentucky.

820
01:14:42,620 --> 01:14:43,640
That's horseshit.

821
01:14:43,980 --> 01:14:45,039
He's getting help.

822
01:14:45,220 --> 01:14:46,053
From who?

823
01:14:46,180 --> 01:14:47,040
